{:edb/db-before-t 2731 :edb/db-after-t 2732 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536044 50 #inst "2026-10-09T13:36:41.890Z" 13194139536044 true] [17592186124487 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380757 13194139536044 true] [17592186124489 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380750 13194139536044 true] [17592186380750 1017 #edb/ref 17592186380751 13194139536044 true] [17592186380750 1089 "q-79841" 13194139536044 true] [17592186380750 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536044 true] [17592186380750 1100 "Estimate $\\sqrt{3.9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.2)$ using a differential $\\text{d}f$ of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y$ at the point $(4,1).$" 13194139536044 true] [17592186380750 1113 #uuid "a13616d8-6843-5639-b89a-041b941279af" 13194139536044 true] [17592186380750 1145 "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{y}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(4,1),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡1}{2\\sqrt{4}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{\\sqrt{4}}{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =0\\,\\text{d}x+2\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(4+Δx,1+Δy),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈0\\,Δx+2\\,Δy\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n\\sqrt{3.9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.2)=f(3.9,1.2),\n$$\n\nso we want to move to the point $(3.9,1.2).$\n\nMoving from $(4,1)$ to $(3.9,1.2),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =3.9-4=-0.1, \\\\ Δy & =1.2-1=0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈0\\cdot (-0.1)+2\\cdot (0.2) \\\\  & ≈0+0.4 \\\\  & ≈0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that the value of $f$ increases by about $0.4.$ Consequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3.9,1.2) & ≈f(4,1)+0.4 \\\\ \\sqrt{3.9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.2) & ≈\\sqrt{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+0.4 \\\\  & ≈0+0.4 \\\\  & ≈0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536044 true] [17592186380751 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380752 13194139536044 true] [17592186380751 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380753 13194139536044 true] [17592186380751 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380754 13194139536044 true] [17592186380751 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380755 13194139536044 true] [17592186380751 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380756 13194139536044 true] [17592186380751 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536044 true] [17592186380751 1041 "selection" 13194139536044 true] [17592186380751 1104 #edb/ref 17592186380754 13194139536044 true] [17592186380751 1110 #uuid "a781bd1b-8b0c-5f28-b4d4-64190d3458ee" 13194139536044 true] [17592186380752 1034 "0.43" 13194139536044 true] [17592186380752 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536044 true] [17592186380752 1111 #uuid "4f5a5b5d-1130-562b-be75-79235b9cd42f" 13194139536044 true] [17592186380753 1034 "0.42" 13194139536044 true] [17592186380753 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536044 true] [17592186380753 1111 #uuid "d99291bd-3f8c-5335-affd-fffd94f5d90e" 13194139536044 true] [17592186380754 1034 "0.40" 13194139536044 true] [17592186380754 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536044 true] [17592186380754 1111 #uuid "7a2258da-1286-500d-b5ea-e5019f6bc9e9" 13194139536044 true] [17592186380755 1034 "0.35" 13194139536044 true] [17592186380755 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536044 true] [17592186380755 1111 #uuid "80c5a22d-851a-5e64-bf18-646fa4b64de5" 13194139536044 true] [17592186380756 1034 "0.38" 13194139536044 true] [17592186380756 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536044 true] [17592186380756 1111 #uuid "2e72d255-ef28-56b9-b614-389fd1c36d2f" 13194139536044 true] [17592186380757 1017 #edb/ref 17592186380758 13194139536044 true] [17592186380757 1089 "q-79959" 13194139536044 true] [17592186380757 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536044 true] [17592186380757 1100 "Given a right cone, find the differential $\\text{d}S$ for the lateral surface area $S$ of the right cone if the base radius is $r=6,$ and the slant height is $l=10.$" 1